# SCENARIO_RUNS above means CUBE's own upstream test suite (18/18) was
# observed passing in this repo's CI. GYMACT_ACTUATED claims below are
# distinct, stronger claims -- GymAct's own kernel (~/gymact, real
# GymAct.materialize/act/observe/verify/teardown) actually drove a real CUBE
# task end to end.
#
# Neither claim is bound to a prose description or a source path -- each is
# bound to its own real OCEL 2.0 log (gymact.ocel.write_ocel_log), built
# directly from the real Receipts that episode produced, schema-valid
# against the real official OCEL 2.0 JSON Schema (vendored at
# ~/gymact/src/gymact/schemas/ocel20-schema.json), with real "date-time"
# format checking (rfc3339-validator) -- not a no-op format check. Each
# digest is computed over the exact bytes of its evidence file; anyone can
# verify either claim themselves with nothing more than `shasum -a 256` on
# the cited path. Re-extracting `events[].type` from either file (sorted by
# real `time`) and feeding it to gymact.process.ConformanceChecker
# reproduces the conformant verdict independently of this file, this repo,
# or anything I have said about it -- see ~/gymact/tests/test_ocel.py::
# test_conformance_verdict_is_re_derivable_from_the_log_alone for the exact
# mechanism. Neither claim has run in CI -- both are local-session standings,
# not GitHub Actions provenance claims. Scope, in full: two CUBE task
# variants (below), not CUBE's full task registry, and still 1 of 80
# ForwardBench subjects -- see docs/plans (autofde-lab session 2026-08-07)
# for the honest 0/80-wired-before -> 1/80-wired-now count.
<https://github.com/seanchatmangpt/autofde-lab/data/forwardbench/vendor-cube-standard>
  afb:gymactActuation <https://github.com/seanchatmangpt/autofde-lab/data/forwardbench/gymact-actuation/counter-cube> ;
  afb:gymactActuation <https://github.com/seanchatmangpt/autofde-lab/data/forwardbench/gymact-actuation/toy-benchmark-container> .

# Claim 1: counter-cube (examples/counter-cube) -- pure in-memory task, no
# infra provisioning. materialize() only constructs a Python object;
# reset()/act() never touch a subprocess, container, or network. 4 real
# receipted operations (materialize, 3x act, teardown = 5 events).
<https://github.com/seanchatmangpt/autofde-lab/data/forwardbench/gymact-actuation/counter-cube>
