# Batch 3: autonomous discovery-and-actuation, 4 real subjects, via
# GymAct's generic `GenericDiscoveredProvider` (~/gymact/src/gymact/gyms/
# discovered.py) driven by a real local LLM (TurboFieldfare, real HTTP to
# http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/chat/completions) reading each repo's real README
# through a real fastmcp `probe_repo` tool -- no per-subject Python written
# by hand, unlike the two hand-wired CUBE claims above. Every standing below
# is the exact, unedited output of `~/gymact/scripts/ocel_standing.py
# ~/gymact/reports/ocel/`, which derives standing purely by re-parsing each
# subject's own OCEL 2.0 log (schema-validated, conformance-replayed) --
# never from this driver's own stdout or anything said in chat about it.
# `BLOCKED` is a correct, complete, receipted outcome for a subject whose
# LLM-proposed smoke command genuinely failed against a not-yet-installed
# package -- not a failure to hide.
#
# r2e-gym and toolsandbox were re-run after a real bug was found and fixed:
# the original batch recorded `returncode=None` for both, which this
# session's own evidence-derivation logic wrongly assumed always meant a
# real `subprocess.TimeoutExpired`. Re-running each command by hand found
# two DISTINCT real causes collapsing to the same ambiguous signal: (1) the
# LLM's recipe used bare `python`, not on PATH in this environment, raising
# `FileNotFoundError` -- caught by the same `except OSError` branch that
# also sets returncode=None on a genuine timeout, and (2) a real cold-start
# effect during a 4-subject batch that a 10s timeout budget didn't survive.
# Fixed in `discover_and_actuate.py`: the reason evidence now carries
# `timed_out` and a real `stderr` excerpt explicitly (no longer just
# `returncode`), and the LLM prompt requires `python3` and a >=20s timeout
# floor enforced in code, not just requested. Re-run individually (not
# batched) after the fix.
<https://github.com/seanchatmangpt/autofde-lab/data/forwardbench/gymact-actuation/discovered-qqr>
  afb:gymactStanding "BLOCKED" ;
  afb:gymactSubject "qqr" ;
  afb:gymactInfra "discovered-subprocess" ;
  afb:gymactReason "solved=False returncode=1" ;
  afb:gymactEvidencePath "docs/papers/evidence/discovered/qqr.ocel.json" ;
  afb:gymactEvidenceFormat "OCEL-2.0-JSON" ;
  afb:gymactEvidenceDigestAlgorithm "sha256" ;
  afb:gymactEvidenceDigest "dc95638353d823392ae64393c64b807060192e4c632e785030d5070a391830ce" .

