# Correction (2026-08-07): a working-backwards press release circulated this
# session claiming "GYMACT_ACTUATED across all 80 ForwardBench subjects...
# zero unknown... zero blocked... process intelligence via wasm4pm." That
# claim was audited this session by 5 parallel Explore agents against the
# real state of this repo and found false on every count it made: real
# GYMACT_ACTUATED standing above covers 3 subjects total (counter-cube,
# toolsandbox/count-to-3-with-decrement, sadservers), not 80; qqr and
# r2e-gym above carry a real BLOCKED standing, so "zero blocked" is false;
# 28 of the 80 registry subjects (see docs/papers/generated/forwardbench/
# registry.json cross-referenced against docs/papers/gym-lock.ttl) have
# never been pinned or resolved at all, so "zero unknown" is false; and no
# wasm4pm-based process intelligence exists anywhere in this repo's
# evidence chain -- conformance above is checked by
# gymact.process.ConformanceChecker (see comment above), not wasm4pm. This
# comment does not alter, delete, or reinterpret any existing triple in
# this file; the GYMACT_ACTUATED and BLOCKED standings recorded above
# remain exactly as they were independently verified. The full audit that
# found the press release false is recorded outside this repo at
# ~/.claude/plans/launch-5-lumen-explore-calm-acorn.md (not a path inside
# this repo; cited for provenance only, not meant to be read as part of
# this file's own evidence chain).

# vendor-terragoat: excluded from GymAct actuation consideration, real reason,
# not a silent drop. Cloned for real this session (lands exactly on the
# already-pinned SHA 729f8da62c6a85ce4af5ad3d123de97776d954c4 in
# gym-lock.ttl). But its .tf files (under terraform/{aws,azure,gcp,alicloud}/)
# use pre-0.12 legacy HCL syntax (quoted type constraints, e.g.
# `type = "string"` in consts.tf) that both installed `terraform` (v1.14.6)
# and `tofu` (v1.10.6) reject at parse time -- confirmed independently
# against both real binaries, real `init -backend=false`, real error output,
# not a guess. This is a genuine tooling-version incompatibility in the
# subject itself, not a GymAct harness gap: TerraformPlanProvider (real,
# working, zero apply capability by design -- see
# gymact/src/gymact/gyms/terraform_plan.py) correctly detects and reports
# this via a real subprocess check, not a stale file-existence proxy (an
# earlier version of that check only tested `.tf` file presence, which
# passed even though `init` genuinely fails -- fixed same session).
# Not pursuing: patching terragoat's vendored .tf files to force
# compatibility would corrupt the pinned checkout and stop testing the real
# subject. No other Terraform-family subject in the corpus has been
# confirmed compatible either; TerraformPlanProvider itself is not
# terragoat-specific and remains available if a compatible Terraform subject
# is added later.
<https://github.com/seanchatmangpt/autofde-lab/data/forwardbench/vendor-terragoat>
  afb:gymactStanding "SUPERSEDED" ;
  afb:gymactReason "the UNSUPPORTED verdict above no longer holds -- see gymact-actuation/terraform-plan-terragoat-alicloud below for the current real evidence" .

# UPDATE, same session: the UNSUPPORTED verdict above was real at the time
# but has been superseded. Found a real upstream fix: bridgecrewio/terragoat
# has an unmerged branch `fix_outdated_tf` (commit
# 6b1c6d4de22f57b0997ebcc70041e175f55de721) that converts exactly the
# quoted-type-constraint syntax to modern HCL -- verified directly (real
# `terraform init` succeeds cleanly against it, real providers downloaded,
# checked in a throwaway git worktree before trusting it). Forked to
# https://github.com/seanchatmangpt/terragoat with `main` re-pointed at that
# commit and set as the fork's default branch (`gh api`/`gh repo edit`,
# independently re-verified via a fresh `git clone --branch main` + real
# `terraform init`). `.gitmodules`/gym-lock.ttl's vendor-terragoat entry now
# point at this fork; the vendored checkout was fully re-cloned (not just
# checked out in place) and its `origin` remote confirmed to be the fork via
# `git submodule sync`.
#
# Two further real, distinct blockers were found and resolved while getting
# an actual passing test, not assumed away:
# 1. `terraform/aws/providers.tf` declares a real S3 remote backend
#    (bucket/key/region required). `TerraformPlanProvider.materialize()`
#    was missing `-backend=false` on its `init` call -- without it, init
#    either fails on missing backend attributes or (if supplied) would mean
#    real Terraform state written to a real AWS S3 bucket, which this
#    plan-only provider must never risk. Fixed in
#    gymact/src/gymact/gyms/terraform_plan.py; its docstring's prior claim
#    ("terragoat declares no remote backend") was simply wrong and is now
#    corrected in-code.
# 2. Even with that fix, `terraform/aws` specifically cannot run a real
#    `plan` locally at all -- `-backend=false` at init leaves the declared
#    S3 backend unresolved, and `plan` then refuses with a real, reproduced
#    "Backend initialization required" error (retested from a fully clean
#    `.terraform` dir, not stale state). This is a structural property of
#    that one cloud subdirectory, not a harness bug. Switched the target to
#    `terraform/alicloud`, which declares no remote backend and has no
#    legacy syntax either -- real `init` and real `plan` both now run to
#    completion there (`test_terraform_plan.py`: 4/4 real tests pass).
#
# Standing is NOT set to GYMACT_ACTUATED below, on purpose. Running
# `ocel_standing.py` (the sole mechanical arbiter for this claim, per this
# session's own discipline) against the real episode's real OCEL log
# reports `BLOCKED`, reason: "act event(s) present but none carry
# solved=True evidence" -- because `ocel_standing.py`'s standing heuristic
# was written for the `discovered` provider family's `solved=` marker
# embedded in receipt.reason, and TerraformPlanProvider never embeds that
# marker (its own real success signal is a `verify()` boolean, not a
# `solved=` string). Worse, found live: `GymAct.verify()` does not emit any
# receipted OCEL event at all -- a real `gym.verify(episode_id, {})` call
# returned `passed: True` in this session's own driver script, but that
# fact exists nowhere in the OCEL log itself, only in this script's stdout.
# That is exactly the class of unreceipted claim this session's own
# discipline exists to catch, so it is not being papered over here: the
# test skip (a harness-code gap) is genuinely closed, but the corpus
# GYMACT_ACTUATED claim is correctly withheld until either (a)
# `GymAct.verify()` is extended to emit a real receipted event, or (b)
# `ocel_standing.py` is extended to recognize a provider-family-appropriate
# success signal beyond the `discovered` family's specific convention.
# Neither fix is in scope here -- named as real follow-up work, not solved.
<https://github.com/seanchatmangpt/autofde-lab/data/forwardbench/gymact-actuation/terraform-plan-terragoat-alicloud>
  afb:gymactStanding "BLOCKED" ;
  afb:gymactSubject "terragoat/terraform/alicloud" ;
  afb:gymactInfra "local-terraform-cli" ;
  afb:gymactReason "act event(s) present but none carry solved=True evidence -- ocel_standing.py's standing heuristic does not yet generalize beyond the discovered-provider family's marker convention, and GymAct.verify() does not emit a receipted OCEL event; real test suite (test_terraform_plan.py) passes 4/4, but that is not the same claim as a mechanically-derived GYMACT_ACTUATED standing" ;
  afb:gymactEvidencePath "docs/papers/evidence/terraform-plan/terragoat-alicloud-episode.ocel.json" ;
  afb:gymactEvidenceFormat "OCEL-2.0-JSON" ;
  afb:gymactEvidenceDigestAlgorithm "sha256" ;
  afb:gymactEvidenceDigest "dbe17a53f128209d06517218581d18c7c1d73d1d0eb004d410907cd043b3b1a1" .
